// B4 (2026-09-30): THE SCHEDULE REACHES A CALLEE'S FANOUT. `both` fans out
// with no install of its own; `main` installs `parallel_compose` over the
// CALL, so the demand reaches `both` through the direct call and its two
// branches run on spawned instances — `current_id()` answers each host
// thread's id, nonzero off the root instance. On boot 6f2ce437 the frame
// fence made a callee's fanout sequential whatever the caller installed:
// both ids were 0 and the program exited 1.
// Expected exit: 14.
fn both() = (current_id()) >< (current_id())
fn main() = match (both()) ~> parallel_compose {
  (a, b) => if a > 0 && b > 0 { 14 } else { 1 },
}
